# Testing Expectations

## Test Scope

- Unit tests for isolated logic and validation rules
- Integration tests for stage orchestration and I/O boundaries
- End-to-end tests for stage pipelines and expected outputs

## Determinism and Fixtures

- Prefer deterministic seed/config-driven tests.
- Use focused fixtures for schema, anomaly, and row-count behavior.
- Avoid machine-specific absolute paths in test logic.

## Data and Schema Validation

- Validate required schemas and data types at stage boundaries.
- Validate expected row-count relationships where required.
- Verify preservation of intentional anomalies for Bronze inputs/outputs.

## Compatibility

- Keep local execution testable where environment permits.
- Preserve Databricks compatibility in design and test assumptions.

## Regression Discipline

- Add or update tests with behavior changes.
- Do not rewrite raw Bronze data to satisfy tests.
- Do not fabricate pass results; report actual outcomes and blockers.
